ut no step describes re-posting from it if a wrong delete is detected.","Jira comment DELETE is server-side irreversible; a restore would create new comment ids/timestamps, so the back-out is non-trivial and should be stated."],"finding":"The T4 safety plan provides a pre-deletion backup but no explicit back-out/restore procedure; a backup enables but is not itself a rollback plan for the irreversible Jira DELETEs.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f01cd891729482e6a","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Safety plan (T4 — irreversible) — 'Pre-deletion backup of the FULL comment payload'","norm_id":"n4094a6c58a222cc8","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Post-verification detects a distinct body lost its only surviving copy on some issue and an operator needs to restore it from backup/<KEY>.json."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a Safety-plan bullet: 'Back-out: if post-verification flags a missing distinct body, re-POST it from backup/<KEY>.json via /rest/api/3/issue/{key}/comment (new id/timestamp; original author noted in body). Deletion is otherwise irreversible; keep-one + dry-run + canary are the primary controls.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"hard","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Document the restore/back-out procedure that consumes backup/<KEY>.json (how bodies are re-posted, that ids/timestamps will differ) and add a DATA LOSS RISK note that deletion is one-way, so the backup is proven-usable rather than merely present.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3637,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Pre-deletion backup of the FULL comment payload ... written and completeness-checked BEFORE any DELETE' — backup is described but no restore path is","Deletion is one-way: re-posting a backed-up ADF body would create a NEW comment id/created timestamp, so 'restore' is not a clean inverse","POST-ROLLBACK STATE overlay applies: this is a one-way transformation with no back-out"],"finding":"The operation is an irreversible bulk DELETE (deleted Jira comments cannot be un-deleted by the script), yet the Safety plan asserts only that a full-payload backup is written and completeness-checked BEFORE any DELETE — it never describes a RESTORE/back-out procedure or asserts the post-restore state would be correct.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4c0a8172671b9737","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Safety plan (T4 — irreversible) — Pre-deletion backup bullet; AC 'backup/<KEY>.json for all 27 issues'","norm_id":"n8a7e8a79173b23d1","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A partial run deletes wrong comments (e.g. a bot/human accountId misclassification slips through), and the operator must reconstruct state from backup/<KEY>.json"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"hard","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify why DELETE cannot route through `_call_with_retry(client.delete_comment, key, id)` (which already retries 429 honoring `Retry-After` and backs off on 5xx), or drop the bespoke wrapper and reuse it — matching the bd80 precedent's 'Do NOT hand-roll a second retry layer'; keep only the per-call throttle as the script-local addition.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4475,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'DELETE does NOT go through delete_comment/_direct_rest_delete, which re-raise 4xx/5xx immediately and would hard-abort on the first 429 ... Every request goes through the script's own wrapper, which honours Retry-After on 429 and backs off exponentially on 5xx/transient faults'","_call_with_retry already catches raw urllib.error.HTTPError, retries 429 honoring a present Retry-After and 5xx with jittered backoff (dispatch_apply_phases.py:113-133) — it re-raises ONLY non-429 4xx","delete_comment -> _direct_rest_delete raises raw HTTPError (acli_rest.py:304-319); wrapping that call in _call_with_retry gives the desired 429/Retry-After behavior, which is exactly what bd80 (extrovert-dippy-bongo) specified: 'wrap each DELETE call through dispatch_one._call_with_retry ... Do NOT hand-roll a second retry layer'","The stated rationale ('re-raise ... would hard-abort on the first 429') is only true when the leaf is called directly, not when wrapped in _call_with_retry — the plan omits the wrap-in-_call_with_retry option its precedent used"],"finding":"The plan hand-rolls 'the script's own wrapper' for DELETE 429/Retry-After + 5xx backoff, duplicating the existing _call_with_retry — and contradicting its own cited bd80 precedent, which routed DELETEs through dispatch_one._call_with_retry and explicitly said 'Do NOT hand-roll a second retry layer'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb9d73557a539f113","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Mechanism section, 'Rate limiting — 429 IS retried, explicitly' bullet","norm_id":"ne5d37b8aea494850","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["~30k DELETEs against Jira Cloud rate limits where a bespoke retry layer must independently and correctly implement Retry-After parsing/capping that _call_with_retry + parse_retry_after already provide","A future 429-handling fix to _call_with_retry silently not applying to this script's private copy"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Route each DELETE as `_call_with_retry(client.delete_comment, key, comment_id)`, treating a raised 404 as idempotent success, and add only the inter-call throttle (sleep) around it — rather than reimplementing Retry-After/backoff. If a genuine gap exists (e.g. per-call throttle or a bounded overall budget across 30k calls that _call_with_retry lacks), state that gap explicitly as the reason for the wrapper.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify or eliminate the divergence from bd80's single retry route: either reuse dispatch_one._call_with_retry (as bd80 mandated) or specify how the bespoke wrapper reads Retry-After off the RESPONSE (not request) headers and is covered by a test mirroring the existing 429/Retry-After held-out pins.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4533,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'DELETE does NOT go through delete_comment/_direct_rest_delete… Every request goes through the script's own wrapper, which honours Retry-After on 429 and backs off exponentially on 5xx.'","bd80 ticket description: 'wrap each DELETE call through dispatch_one._call_with_retry, which is the repo's one existing 429+Retry-After-aware retry… Do NOT hand-roll a second retry layer.'","Codebase: parse_retry_after (_errors.py:33) and dispatch_apply_phases.py:121 read Retry-After off exc.headers/response; a hand-rolled wrapper must replicate the response-vs-request-header subtlety pinned by tests (test_dc_rate_limit_retry_heldout.py)."],"finding":"The plan asserts a NEW capability — 'the script's own wrapper' that honours Retry-After on 429 and backs off on 5xx — explicitly diverging from the bd80 precedent it claims to reuse, where bd80 routed every DELETE through the repo's single existing retry (dispatch_one._call_with_retry) and stated 'Do NOT hand-roll a second retry layer.' The wrapper is described but not grounded in any existing, tested implementation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f34fb207d9f1ea473","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Mechanism — 'Rate limiting — 429 IS retried, explicitly' bullet","norm_id":"nbfeb28514bb277f2","priority":0.4467,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The bespoke wrapper reads Retry-After from exc.headers instead of the response (a known repo footgun documented in retry.py) and silently never honours it, degrading to a fixed backoff across ~30k deletes."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Prefer routing DELETE through dispatch_one._call_with_retry per bd80; if a bespoke wrapper is truly needed (e.g., for per-call throttle), state that it delegates the 429/Retry-After/5xx retry to the existing helper rather than reimplementing it.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item '[non-codebase] Affected-issue list derived by the documented command from run 32' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] Per issue `len(fetched) == total` held and a backup existed BEFOR' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] Dry run produced and inspected before `--execute` (`logs/dryrun-a' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] Marker detection ran PRE-STRIP — 30,847 `marked` counted; detecti' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] Every DELETE honoured `Retry-After` on 429 — 713+ throttles absor' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] Every issue below the cap; REB-1861 5000 -> 79 (`logs/final-verif' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] Post-deletion re-fetch shows zero missing distinct bodies and unc' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] Deletion log has one object per deletion: 29,931 lines in' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the Jira authorization precondition explicitly: confirm the bot account holds the project 'Delete all comments' permission (verified on the canary before the full run), and define 403-on-DELETE handling distinctly from the idempotent 404 case.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'A 404 on DELETE is idempotent success, so re-runs are safe' — addresses 404 but not 403.","Codebase _direct_rest_delete (acli_rest.py:304-320) uses Basic auth (user:api_token) over HTTPS; permission is a server-side project grant, orthogonal to auth working.","ABSENCE: no plan text asserts the bot has Jira delete-comment permission, and the canary step verifies deletion outcome but does not pre-flight the permission."],"finding":"The plan depends on DELETE /rest/api/3/issue/{key}/comment/{id} succeeding across ~30k calls but never states the authorization precondition: the bot account must hold the Jira project 'Delete all comments' permission. Endpoint existence (confirmed in acli_graph.py) does not imply the token is permitted to delete. A 403 (insufficient permission) is a different failure than the idempotent 404 the plan handles.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2049de84514ea305","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Mechanism — 'Rate limiting — 429 IS retried' bullet / Safety plan","norm_id":"n412c5c056cbac7e4","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The bot token can POST comments (proven by the bug) but the project's comment-delete permission was never granted to it, so the very first DELETE (canary) returns 403 and the whole operation is blocked after backup."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add an auth/permission precondition line ('bot accountId 712020:6471376f… holds Delete-all-comments on the target project, verified by the canary DELETE') and specify that a 403 aborts the issue rather than being treated as idempotent success.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"664166cec1766574","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["d8349cad625a121d",7998],"description_boxes":["8108ed602688b707",14],"file_impact":["003ffa614d5e4a28",0],"file_impact_scope":["9001e8b2a5a6bd74",2],"ticket_id":["54ac15d9627010c9",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":4829.8,"input_tokens":944848,"llm_calls":28,"llm_ms":224983.6,"output_tokens":26857,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":232552.7,"verify_requests":11},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":"none","supports_temperature":true,"supports_thinking":true,"web_access":"off"},"endpoint_host":null,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider":"bedrock","ran_model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","region":"us-west-2","region_source":"AWS_REGION","tier":"first_class"},"regver":"362a5dd2d2052826","review_phase":"planning","reviewed_related_material":[],"runner":"pydantic_ai","schema":"plan_review_result_v2","source":"attested","ticket_id":"76b2-4b5f-5682-45e5","ticket_type":"task","verdict":"PASS","verified_at_sha":"8fa8f36b6482b2371128607a63c5483a9783e887"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"REVIEW_RESULT","timestamp":1787272976504359001,"uuid":"1cba1bfd-04a4-4564-8dd2-d085237122c4"}